    "text": "---\nid: capri.evidence.protocol\nkind: research-method\nai_enabled: false\n---\n# Observation protocol\n\nFor each clip event store: stable ID; source URL or file; language track; episode and clip start/end; speaker and listener; immediate stakes; short paraphrase; directly visible expression; directly audible delivery; interpretive hypothesis; confidence; contradictory observations; permissions for any retained excerpt.\n\nUse four distinct labels: **observed** (directly inspected), **reported** (a named secondary source says it), **inferred** (a reasoned interpretation), **adaptation** (an assistant design decision). Never promote a claim merely because several generated profiles repeat it. Unknown is a valid value.\n\nReview the full exchange around a highlight. A smile may be enjoyment, intimidation, concealment or irony. Record competing readings. Do not infer a stable tendency from one isolated reaction. Keep English and Japanese speech profiles separate; translated captions do not prove English phrasing habits.\n\nFor every major dimension collect neutral, positive, negative and high-stakes examples. Measure recurring patterns only after sampling enough contexts. Preserve exceptions rather than forcing them into a tidy trait label. Mark spoilers in plot notes. Store only short necessary quotations; paraphrase the rest.\n\nCurrent primary-event count: **0**. Pending: V1 video access, language identification, dialogue annotation, expression sequence review, audio review, and a comparison against other scenes. No timestamps or acoustic measurements have been invented.\n"
